    description: "STATEMENT\nA Kotlin call to a class or function of the caller's own package (visible without an import), or one a qualifier names, binds that declaration and not a same-named one of another package.\n\nOBSERVED (2026-11-25; blinded sample judged from source, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/sample_11252026/results.md; okhttp; 8 wrong of 56 judged, all 8 \"another declaration of this repository\")\n- Four calls in files of package mockwebserver3 (`MockWebServer()`, `MockResponse()`, `.enqueue`, `.close`) are bound to the same-named classes of okhttp3.mockwebserver in the mockwebserver-deprecated module. The caller's own package declares the class; no import names the other.\n- `Platform()` called inside package okhttp3.internal.platform is bound to a class `Platform` nested in UrlComponentEncodingTester (not visible from the call site), twice.\n- `Headers.Builder()` and `Request.Builder()` are bound to MockResponse.Builder (mark class_hint): the qualifier the call writes is not used.\nBy stratum: name with several candidates 4 wrong of 15; receiver_type whose owner name is shared 2 of 6; class_hint 2 of 3. With one candidate: 0 wrong of 20.\nKotlin has no guess cell in the call-resolution fixture: the fixture has no same-named class in two packages."  # 733c
